    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "House of Voronov is a noble house of the Tsardom of Velikhor, a cold northern realm ruled by the Tsar from the frozen capital of Novgrad.",
      "since": 947
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The house takes its name from the great grey owl depicted on its shield, a bird sacred to the owl-folk of Velikhor, believed to be messengers between the living and the dead.",
      "since": 947
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Voronovs rose to prominence in the reign of Tsar Dmitri II by providing crucial military leadership during the Frostborn Campaigns against the southern Khaelid Khanate.",
      "since": 947
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Their seat is the fortress of Snegovaya Krepost, a towering stone keep built into the cliffs above the frozen river Vostok, in the northern province of Koldunya.",
      "since": 947
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The current head of the house is Prince Aleksei Voronov, a shrewd diplomat and skilled warrior who serves as Lord Steward of the northern marches.",
      "since": 1000
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Voronovs are known for their owl-folk heritage: every firstborn child of the house is said to be born with unnaturally large, luminous eyes and an intuitive sense for danger, traits they share with the owl-folk tribes of the northern wilderness.",
      "since": 947
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Their family motto is 'We Watch, We Wait, We Strike' — carved into the archway of Snegovaya Krepost above the main gate.",
      "since": 947
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Voronovs hold vast estates in Koldunya, including grain fields, hunting forests, and iron mines, making them one of the wealthiest houses in Velikhor.",
      "since": 947
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Prince Aleksei's eldest daughter, Yelena Voronova, is renowned across the tsardom for her skill in falconry and her sharp mind, and is often called 'the Owl's Eye.'",
      "since": 1000
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The house maintains a private library at Snegovaya Krepost containing rare texts on owl-folk shamanism, northern warfare, and the ancient history of Velikhor before the Tsars.",
      "since": 962
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Every winter solstice, the Voronovs host the Pale Feast, a grand gathering where northern lords and owl-folk chieftains come together to forge alliances and settle disputes.",
      "since": 947
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Voronovs have a long-standing rivalry with House Chernyavsky, another powerful noble family of Velikhor, rooted in a territorial dispute over the iron mines of Koldunya that has never been fully resolved.",
      "since": 973
    }
  ],
